From 000000000000000000000000000000000000000b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: husky-port CI <ci@husky-port.local>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DIAGNOSTIC: noop exynos_usbdrd_s2mpu_manual_control (freeze bisect)

Every build where the S2MPU allow-all bypass is actually written
(lazy-link on r12: 5/5 boots; lazy-link on r8: 1/1; rtpm-style
pm_runtime variant on r8: 1/1) hard-freezes at ~6.1-6.45s, right at the
moment stock kernels die with the HSI0 SysMMU panic (~6.4-6.47s, first
USB gadget DMA).  The manual_control CODE PATH is now exonerated:
pm_runtime vs raw notify pointer both freeze, and removing the
device-tree lookup changed nothing.

Hypothesis: the first gadget DMA is the killer in both cases.  With
S2MPU blocking (stock) the DMA faults -> clean panic with logs.  With
the bypass ACTIVE the DMA proceeds - and if it targets a bogus address
it silently corrupts kernel memory -> total freeze with zero logs.

This patch makes manual_control() a complete no-op (S2MPU stays in its
boot state, no bypass writes ever).  Predicted outcome if the
hypothesis holds: NO freeze; the stock SysMMU panic returns at ~6.4s.
If the freeze persists even with the no-op, the entire S2MPU theory is
wrong and the cause is elsewhere in the build.
---
diff --git a/soc/gs/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-exynos-usbdrd-eusb.c b/soc/gs/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-exynos-usbdrd-eusb.c
index 80b291b..c8d6104 100644
--- a/soc/gs/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-exynos-usbdrd-eusb.c
+++ b/soc/gs/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-exynos-usbdrd-eusb.c
@@ -1858,25 +1858,13 @@ static int exynos_usbdrd_phy_power_off(struct phy *phy)
 
 int exynos_usbdrd_s2mpu_manual_control(bool on)
 {
-	struct exynos_usbdrd_phy *phy_drd;
-	int (*__s2mpu_notify)(struct device *dev, bool on);
-
-	pr_debug("%s s2mpu = %d\n", __func__, on);
-
-	phy_drd = exynos_usbdrd_get_struct();
-
-	if (!phy_drd) {
-		pr_err("[%s] exynos_usbdrd_get_struct error\n", __func__);
-		return -ENODEV;
-	}
-
-	/* Paired with cmpxchg_release in exynos_usbdrd_set_s2mpu_pm_ops. */
-	__s2mpu_notify = smp_load_acquire(&s2mpu_notify);
-	if (!phy_drd->s2mpu || !__s2mpu_notify)
-		return 0;
-
-	__s2mpu_notify(phy_drd->s2mpu, on);
-
+	/*
+	 * DIAGNOSTIC (freeze bisect): complete no-op.  Never touch the
+	 * S2MPU.  If the ~6.3s total freeze disappears (and the stock
+	 * SysMMU panic at first gadget DMA returns instead), then the
+	 * freeze is caused by the S2MPU allow-all bypass being ACTIVE,
+	 * not by any manual_control code path.
+	 */
 	return 0;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(exynos_usbdrd_s2mpu_manual_control);

